works: This time the answer is yes; {N} reads it standing at the kitchen window, reads it again, and walks twice round the block before telling anyone.
works: Whatever {N} chose, the second time feels different: steadier, and entirely {Ns} own.
fails: It is the same kind of no as last time, nearly to the word, and {N} finds that it stings less, and is glad to have gone back at all.
fails: The work gets further than before, and one person who matters says one true thing about it; {N} goes home the long way, in no hurry at all.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- making peace with it (cross cycle s3)
# What the attempt gave, years on: a class kept for years (W, [pupils who remember you]), the choosing taught from the
# inside (U), the story told well (B), a weekly life class for the joy of it (R, `title: life-drawing regular`, an
# entry rung open to anyone and the start of the road back), a circle of the old class and the new (G, [a circle of
# artists]). The cross cycle at 78: a fair list at the open-mic night, the lesson written down for the class, a small
# prize for the town's young artists, the attempt itself painted, the old work given to the town hall. Here the
# anti-story pays off: the peace reading and the Book of Moments can name the long shot.

== the long shot becomes a class to teach
tier: echo
rate: 0.05
once: yes
stages: young_adult adult mature elder
age: 25-100
times: per person who missed an art, craft or writing long shot: about 1 in 10 come to teach or tell it years later, in a class, a workshop or a circle (estimate); most people who teach drawing or writing to adult beginners once tried for something bigger themselves (estimate)
tone: joy
life: meaning, friends, making
horizon: years
roles: friend, partner, colleague, mentor
earth: years after the long shot that missed, the library asks for a Saturday class for adult beginners, and the story comes into the room with the teacher
tribal: winters after the attempt that failed, the young ones of the band ask to learn the marks, and the telling of the attempt comes with them
magic: years after the attempt that failed, the ward's guildhall asks for a class for grown beginners on rest days, and the tale of it comes with the teacher
after: a long shot missed in one of the moments of art-longshots.lib (as for 'the same canvas, years later'), holding [a long shot that missed]; now 25 or more, not a [renowned artist] or a [celebrated author]
delay: 5-30
likelier: years gone by since the attempt; teaching, a class or a circle kept up; much White and Green in the colour history
rarer: stress above 1.5; poor health
scene: Years after the long shot that missed, the library asks {N} to run a class for adult beginners on Saturday mornings, ten weeks, drawing or writing, whichever {N} likes. On the first morning, before anyone has picked up a pencil, a woman of sixty asks whether {N} ever tried to make it big. The room goes quiet to hear the answer.
scene W: {N} tells it straight: what was asked, what {N} sent, and the letter that said no. Then the register is taken and the class starts on time, because that is how a class should run.
scene U: Over the years {N} has understood that attempt better than at the time: what the people choosing were looking for, and what {N} had not yet learned. That is worth teaching, more than any technique.
scene B: It has become a good story, and {N} knows how to tell it: the long odds, the nerve, the near thing at the end. A class remembers a teacher with a story.
scene R: The ache has mostly gone, and what is left is the memory of the nerve it took. {N} would like every beginner in the room to feel that once.
scene G: The attempt is part of {Ns} life now, like the old house and the long friendships. What matters this morning is the man at the back who has never drawn a line and whose hands are shaking.
scene tribal: One winter the young ones of the band ask {N} to show them the marks at the painting place, and one of them asks whether it is true that {N} once took a hide to the elders and was turned away. The young ones go quiet to hear the telling.
scene magic: The ward's guildhall asks {N} to teach grown beginners on rest days, and on the first morning an old weaver asks whether {N} once tried for the academy's great hall. The class goes quiet to hear the tale.
