works: The class fills up for a second term and a third, and years later strangers stop {N} in the street to say they still draw, or write, because of a Saturday morning at the library.
works: Whatever {N} chose, the old attempt has found its place in the life, and {N} no longer flinches when it comes up.
fails: The class shrinks to three by the fifth week, and {N} teaches those three as well as {N} has ever done anything.
fails: Someone asks whether it was worth it, an answer comes out sharper than {N} meant, and {N} thinks about it on the bus home for a week.
